{
  "domain": "examples/pizzas",
  "note": "Where-less declared queries on Pizzas::Order, held to the frozen expect on both runtimes. Six orders are created so identity order (alpha..foxtrot) and the declared orders visibly differ: prices 1200/900/1200/1500/900/1500 give ties in every price bucket, which keep identity order; three orders are bought (alpha by Zed, charlie by Amy, echo by Amy) and three stay unbought, so customer_name is unset on bravo, delta and foxtrot. Everything has no where and no order_by (every order, by identity). ByPrice and ByPriceDescending are where-less with a dotted order_by through two value objects, ascending and descending, with ties in identity order in both directions. ByCustomer (ascending, native null placement: unset first), ByCustomerDescending (native: unset last) and ByCustomerUnsetLast (ascending with nulls :last) pin the nil ordering rules, and the two customers named Amy tie and keep identity order. Available keeps the where-bearing path in the same answer.",
